**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlanJobTests`

**How to implement.** `RunPlan` runs off the UI thread on `JobRunner` with per-candidate progress and Cancel (001 §P `RunPlan`; the S14.2 brief 'RunPlan on JobRunner with per-candidate progress'; .spec-md §10.2, §10.3 one click with Cancel, §10.4 'the job's completion message updates the Elmish model, so … the plan view re-render[s] without a manual reload'). It hosts the plan as step 393 hosts a study fit, over `JobRunner.fs:startBackground`, `:updateJob` and `:JobModel`. A plan writes no kit file; its only write is the cache, which a read-only kit does not take (step 485). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `MeasurementPlanner.fs`: `PlannerError` gains `PlanRaisedErr` (`the plan raised: <reason>`) and `UnknownPlannerStudyErr` (`the kit has no such study: <reason>`). (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/PlanJob.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.PlanJob`, compiled directly after `StudyFitJob.fs` (step 393): one `<Compile>` line, no comment. In order: (a) `[<ReferenceEquality>] PlanJobHandle = { cancelPlan : unit -> unit }`. (b) `[<ReferenceEquality>] PlanJobHost = { startPlan : (PlanObserver -> Result<PlanReport, PlannerError>) -> PlanJobHandle }`, with `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<PlanReport, PlannerError> -> unit) : PlanJobHost`: a `CancellationTokenSource` and a `Stopwatch` per job; the plan runs through `JobRunner.startBackground` as `RanToCompletion [ plan o ]`, `o` posting each `PlanProgress` p as `progressed { completed = JobStepCount p.evaluated.value; total = Some (JobStepCount p.total.value); elapsed = JobElapsed <the stopwatch's elapsed> }` (a known total, which `progressText` shows as `<k> / <n> (<t> s)`, `JobRunner.fs:JobModel`) over the source's token; `onDone` posts `ended` of the plan's result, a raise (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ending as `Error (PlanRaisedErr e.Message)` and an outcome holding no result as `Error (PlanRaisedErr <a reason naming it>)`; the handle cancels the source. `static member onUiThread (progressed) (ended) : PlanJobHost` is `posting` through Avalonia's `Dispatcher.UIThread.Post`, and `static member inert : PlanJobHost` runs nothing and answers a handle that does nothing (`StudyFitJobHost.inert`'s shape, step 412). (c) `PlanJobState = { job : JobModel<PlanReport>; handleOpt : PlanJobHandle option; errorOpt : PlannerError option }` with `static member idle`. (d) `PlanRequest = { study : StudyName; material : MaterialVersionId; criterion : PlanCriterion }`. (e) `PlanMsg` = `RunPlan of request : PlanRequest` (the semantic message `PlanRunButton` and the tests send, 001 §P) | `CancelPlan` | `PlanProgressed of progress : JobProgress` | `PlanEnded of result : Result<PlanReport, PlannerError>`, each case documented. (f) `[<ReferenceEquality>] PlanEnvironment = { host : PlanJobHost; planWith : PlanRequest -> PlanObserver -> Result<PlanReport, PlannerError> }`, with `static member create (host : PlanJobHost) (kit : KitContext) (forward : StudyForwardContext) : PlanEnvironment`, whose `planWith request observer` takes the study of `forward.kit.studies` named `request.study` (none: `UnknownPlannerStudyErr`), its `plannerInputsWith forward.kit forward.choiceOf request.material` (step 471), and answers `inputs.planWith forward request.study request.material request.criterion rowsOf observer` (step 486), `rowsOf c` being `inputs.cacheKeyWith forward.kit.items c` bound to `kit.cachedPlannerRows key (fun () -> inputs.candidateRowsWith forward.solverParameters c)` (steps 485, 486). (g) `type PlanMsg with member this.updateWith (environment : PlanEnvironment) (state : PlanJobState) : PlanJobState`: `RunPlan r` while `state.job.isRunning` changes nothing (one plan at a time) and otherwise starts `environment.planWith r` through `environment.host.startPlan`, the job through `updateJob StartRequested`, holding the handle and clearing the error; `CancelPlan` calls the handle's `cancelPlan` while the job runs; `PlanProgressed p` is `updateJob (ProgressReported p)`; `PlanEnded (Ok report)` is `updateJob (RunCompleted report)` with no handle and no error; `PlanEnded (Error (PlanCancelledErr _))` is `updateJob RunCancelled` with no handle, the committed report kept; any other error returns the job to `Idle` with its committed report kept and holds the error. No queue, retry, second job or option is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlanJobTests.fs`, `module PlanJobTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over a host `posting` whose `post` calls at once and whose `progressed` and `ended` feed `PlanProgressed` and `PlanEnded` back through `updateWith`, test-local `planWith` stubs answering a test-local report, and waits on a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep (`StudyFitJobTests`' pattern, step 393): `RunPlan reports each candidate against the total and commits the report once the plan completes`: a stub reporting 1 of 2 and 2 of 2 then answering the report leaves the state `Completed` with that report committed and a progress text starting `2 / 2`; `a cancelled plan keeps the last committed report`: after a completed run, a stub waiting until its observer's cancellation is requested and answering `PlanCancelledErr`, sent `CancelPlan`, leaves the state `Cancelled` with the first report still committed; `a plan that raises ends with PlanRaisedErr carrying its message`: a stub raising `InvalidOperationException "solver gone"` ends with `PlanRaisedErr` holding `solver gone`; `RunPlan while a plan runs starts nothing`: a second `RunPlan` while the first stub waits starts no second plan; `the plan environment caches the kit's candidates under .oc/planner, and a read-only kit caches nothing`: `PlanEnvironment.create` over a read-write in-memory kit holding `PlanRunTests`' study runs the real plan to a report and leaves two `.oc/planner/*.candidate-json` files, and over the same folder opened read-only runs it to an equal report, writing nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the job lands, `PlanMsg.updateWith` MUST run one plan at a time off the UI thread through the host with per-candidate progress against the total, commit its report on completion, keep the last report on Cancel, hold any other error, and `PlanEnvironment.create` MUST plan the named study's material through the kit's cache; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunPlan reports each candidate against the total and commits the report once the plan completes`, `a cancelled plan keeps the last committed report`, `a plan that raises ends with PlanRaisedErr carrying its message`, `RunPlan while a plan runs starts nothing` and `the plan environment caches the kit's candidates under .oc/planner, and a read-only kit caches nothing`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
